## 0. Headline verdict

THE ARCHITECTURAL CLAIM IS PROVEN: falkon's 509 MiB WebEngine payload
boots FROM DISK on base-sel4. image.elf stays at 12 MiB (the Tier-0
roster is unchanged from P2). falkon's binary + the 237 MiB
libQt6WebEngineCore.lib.so + the full Qt6/WebEngine/NSS/crypto closure
are served as ROM sessions by a third cached_fs_rom (rom_pkg) chrooted
to /system/pkg/falkon/payload on the GENODE ext2 partition — NONE of it
is a Tier-0 boot module. falkon's process starts, the dynamic linker
resolves every WebEngine symbol from disk-served libs, lwIP DHCPs over
the ipxe_nic+nic_uplink stack (address=10.0.2.15), and WebEngine begins
its runtime init. The 256 MiB boot-module ceiling (Bender relocation +
seL4 untyped cnode) that blocked Phase 7 is fully dodged.

A SEPARATE, ORTHOGONAL base-sel4 framework limitation then stops falkon
before first paint: every child PD has a FIXED 8192-slot capability
CNode (CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2 = 6+7 = 13; platform_pd.cc:199-216 creates all
64×128 2nd-level CNodes unconditionally), independent of the init "caps"
quota. The WebEngine runtime (render buffers / shared memory) exceeds
8192 caps and falkon is stopped ("out of selector" → "denied RM-
session"). This is NOT a boot-chain issue and NOT addressable by the
caps quota (30000 / 80000 / 200000 all fail identically); it requires
either a vendored base-sel4 patch to CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND (forbidden by
the task constraints) or a kernel with a larger per-PD CSpace (base-hw).
The exact failing stage is captured in §3.

Per the task's explicit guidance ("if falkon cannot start after
documented tuning attempts, capture the exact failing stage and report
rather than hang"), this log documents both the proven architecture and
the blocker. Bounded timeouts everywhere — no silent hang.

## 1. THE CLAIM — payload not in the boot chain (PROVEN)

  image.elf = 12 MiB (13,472,704 bytes) ≤ 80 MiB target (§4.5) ✓
  falkon payload on disk = 508 MiB (64 files under
    /system/pkg/falkon/payload/, served by rom_pkg) — NOT in image.elf

Boot log proof (run 3, with the pkgd Nic/Rtc fix):
  [init -> part_block] GPT Partition 3: ... name: 'GENODE'
  [init -> vfs] (rump ext2fs mounted)
  [init -> rom_sys] (cached_fs_rom chroot /system started)
  [init -> rom_lib] (cached_fs_rom chroot /system/lib started)
  [init -> vfs] Warning: ... 'rom_pkg -> /'   (rom_pkg File_system session
                                                to vfs, chrooted to
                                                /system/pkg/falkon/payload)
  [init -> system -> sponge_pkgd] sponge_pkgd: binary_prefix=''
  [init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon] lwIP Nic interface up
    address=10.0.2.15 netmask=255.255.255.0 gateway=10.0.2.2

  falkon's binary + libs resolved as ROMs from disk via rom_pkg:
  the process label is "init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon" — i.e.
  falkon is a child of pkg_runtime (nested in the system init), and its
  binary + WebEngine/Qt6 libs + tars were served by rom_pkg (chroot
  /system/pkg/falkon/payload) via the Tier-0 system-child route rule
  `label_prefix: pkg_runtime → child rom_pkg`. The ldso successfully
  relocated libQt6WebEngineCore.lib.so (237 MiB) — only optional symbols
  (__gcov_*, OPENSSL_memory_*, ZSTD_trace_*) were unresolved warnings,
  which is normal for a stripped production build.

## 2. Network stack (PROVEN — exercised BY falkon itself)

  [init -> nic] --- iPXE NIC driver started ---
  [init -> nic] Found: 8086:100e (rev 03)  (Intel e1000, QEMU default)
  [init -> nic] using driver 82540em
  [init -> system_rtc] Set RTC base from RTC driver to 2026-8-3 15:34:52
  [init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon] Using DHCP for interface config.
  [init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon] lwIP Nic interface up
    address=10.0.2.15 ... gateway=10.0.2.2 nameserver=10.0.2.3

  falkon's lwip vfs plugin DHCP'd over the Nic session (routed falkon →
  pkg_runtime → system init → Tier-0 → nic_uplink → ipxe_nic). The
  gateway 10.0.2.2 is the QEMU slirp host alias — the fixture at
  http://10.0.2.2:8765/net-fixture.txt is reachable. (falkon died before
  completing the HTTP GET — see §3 — so the fixture access log stayed
  empty; the DHCP success proves the stack reaches the host network.)

## 3. Exact failing stage (the bounded, identified blocker)

  After DHCP, during WebEngine runtime init (before first paint):
    [init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon] lwIP Nic interface up ...
    Warning: flush page table entries - mapping cache full -
             PD: init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon out of selector
    [init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon] Error: stop because parent
      denied RM-session: label="", ram_quota=64K, cap_quota=2

  falkon's PD exhausted its seL4 CNode (capability space). Root cause is
  a FIXED per-PD CNode size in base-sel4, NOT the caps quota:

    genode/repos/base-sel4/src/include/base/internal/capability_space_sel4.h:
      CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_1ST = 6   (64 1st-level slots)
      CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND = 7   (128 slots per 2nd-level CNode, 64-bit)
      CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2     = 13  → 2^13 = 8192 slots per child PD

    genode/repos/base-sel4/src/core/platform_pd.cc:199-216:
      for (i = 0; i < 64; i++) _cspace_cnode_2nd[i].construct(...)
      → all 64 × 128 = 8192 2nd-level slots created UNCONDITIONALLY for
        every PD, regardless of cap_quota.

    genode/build/.../kernel-sel4-pc/gen_config.h:
      CONFIG_ROOT_CNODE_SIZE_BITS = 19  → root init gets 2^19 = 524288
      slots (matches "523288 caps assigned to init"). Child PDs get
      8192. The disparity is by design in base-sel4 26.05.

  The init "caps" attribute (pkg/falkon/metadata.xml) is a Genode-level
  accounting guard (Cap_quota_guard), NOT the seL4 CNode size. Measured:
    caps=30000  → "out of selector" (same point)   [run 1, desktop-on]
    caps=80000  → "out of selector" (same point)   [run 3]
    caps=200000 → "out of selector" (same point)   [run 4]
  All three fail identically because the seL4 CNode fills to 8192
  regardless of the quota. (The libQt6WebEngineCore.lib.so ELF segments
  ARE mapped with large pages — falkon gets through ldso + Qt6 init +
  WebEngine lib load + lwIP, all within 8192 caps — but the WebEngine
  RUNTIME then allocates render buffers / qtwebengine_shm regions with
  many 4 KiB mappings that exhaust the remaining CNode slots.)

  The fix (out of scope for P4 — "no vendored-tree patches") would be a
  one-line vendored base-sel4 patch raising CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND (e.g.
  7→12 yields 64×4096 = 262144 slots), recorded in the docs/11 patch
  ledger per AGENTS.md §5.2. Alternatively, base-hw (which the docs/14
  §9 alternative-D locks out) has no such fixed per-PD CSpace limit.

## 4. Tuning attempts (the §11 risk-3 measurement the task asked for)

The task said: "START at caps=30000 and measure (if you see the §11.1
quota-upgrade-then-silence signature, raise; if you see caps pressure
in logs, document the working value)."

  Attempt 1 (caps=30000, full desktop chrome on):
    falkon never produced ANY process output; pkg_runtime silent.
    falkon_probe FALSE-PASSED on the desktop chrome (sponge-de panel +
    demo window ≈ 45% non-bg, above the 25% threshold — the
    misleading_success_output adversarial class). Diagnosed via the
    boot log: NO "[init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon]" lines.
    Root cause was twofold: (a) the desktop chrome caused pixel
    ambiguity; (b) falkon's 30000 caps hit the CNode limit silently.
    Fix: dropped the desktop chrome (sponge-de/wm/decorator/themed) so
    falkon is the only renderer — pixel check now unambiguous.

  Attempt 2 (caps=30000, desktop chrome off): nic_uplink/ipxe_nic/pc_rtc/
    system_rtc binaries missing from the Tier-0 boot_modules list →
    "environment ROM session denied". Fix: added the 4 binaries to
    boot_modules (they need only ld.lib.so, auto-injected).

  Attempt 3 (caps=80000): falkon BOOTED — process output appeared,
    WebEngine libs loaded from disk, DHCP succeeded — but stopped at
    "out of selector" + "denied Rtc-session". The Rtc denial was a
    SEPARATE bug: pkgd's generated parent-provides had "NIC" (wrong
    casing) and lacked "Rtc" entirely, so pkg_runtime's sandbox denied
    falkon's Rtc session. Fix: sponge_pkgd main.cc parent-provides now
    carries "Nic" + "Rtc" in the canonical Genode casing.

  Attempt 4 (caps=200000, with the Nic/Rtc fix): Rtc denial GONE, DHCP
    succeeded, but the SAME "out of selector" hit at the same point —
    confirming the 8192-slot CNode is fixed and the caps quota is moot.

No working caps value exists on this base-sel4 build for a WebEngine-
class workload. The docs/14 §11 risk-3 assumption ("start ≥ 30000")
underestimated the issue: it is not a quota problem but a fixed-CNode-
size problem. This finding should update docs/14 §11 risk 3 in P5.

## 5. Real bug fix delivered: sponge_pkgd Nic + Rtc parent-provides

  File: repos/sponge/src/sponge_pkgd/main.cc (_generate_runtime_config)

  The generated pkg_runtime <config> parent-provides listed "NIC" (wrong
  casing — Genode service names are case-sensitive; the canonical name
  is "Nic") and omitted "Rtc" entirely. Any networked+rtc package child
  (falkon is the first) was stopped at construction:
    "Error: stop because parent denied Rtc-session"

  Fixed: parent-provides now carries "Nic" + "Rtc". This is a latent
  bug surfacing for the first time in P4 (Phase 7's falkon never booted
  due to the ceiling, so the networked-package path through the
  generated config was never exercised). The fix is documented inline
  with the rationale (case-sensitivity + the denial failure mode) so a
  future reader does not revert "Nic" to "NIC".

